# Official-client scoped account lifecycle and strict HTTP integration patch.
# Target: rustdesk/rustdesk 092a961b629d318fe290eeafac0cd214a1e9deeb.
# Apply from the pinned client's flutter/ directory with git apply.
# Scope: nine exact-pin Dart files plus three integration-owned Dart helpers.
# No full application, generated binding, manifest, runner or media/input path
# is included. model.dart changes only its account-audit consumer and import.
# The real password/verification/OIDC, legacy/shared address-book CRUD, group
# pagination and UI layouts remain official Dart business, not Rust rewrites.
#
# Integration adaptations (not claimed to be upstream transplants):
# - An async atomic native snapshot captures receipt/API/token/user-info and
#   separate Ab/Group cache receipts. Local generation checks supplement, never
#   replace, native authoritative receipt comparison across windows/processes.
# - A bounded account-write/transition queue drains already-submitted native
#   work. Deferred continuations retain the originating lease, not a later
#   getter's credentials. Only the same successful mutation adopts a successor.
# - Cache load/model publication checks the originating kind receipt. Saves and
#   clears use that kind's CAS receipt and retain only their returned successor.
#   Ab deserialize remains model-only; cache clear does not log out the account.
# - OIDC start retains its returned attempt for every poll/cancel. Success may
#   adopt only a snapshot matching returned account_scope and response token.
# - Logout keeps old URL/headers/receipt through its reset; foreign/newer login
#   cannot be cleared by a delayed logout response. Trust/server changes drain
#   the local queue before the official ordered option writes.
# - Native and optional non-web Dart HTTP require captured-scope HTTPS, reject
#   redirects and never override certificate trust. Native enforcement remains
#   required. Sensitive response/body/user-info/header/query diagnostics are
#   removed; authorized business response data is preserved.
#
# Approved additive bridge prerequisites (Main owns paired code generation):
# mainAccountSnapshot; mainAccountSetLocalOption; mainAccountCache;
# mainAccountAuthScoped; mainAccountAuthCancelScoped; mainAccountAuthResultScoped.
# Legacy native account mutation/cache/OIDC entrypoints must fail explicitly.
# No new Dart dependency, request ID, generated API shim or plaintext fallback.
# The conditional web helper keeps the actual upstream JavaScript business
# bridge and user-gesture OIDC ordering; it does not invent native receipts or
# claim a new rd-engine web backend/native protected-storage implementation.
#
